# Product Invariants

- Never modify the original Among Us installation.
- Install each mod beside the detected game in its own stable folder.
- Only uninstall folders containing a valid launcher ownership record.
- Keep updates atomic: stage the new install, swap it into place, and retain the
  previous working copy if promotion fails.
- Treat protected game locations such as Program Files explicitly; show an
  actionable error instead of silently changing the destination.
- Keep install state tied to the selected mod release versus the recorded
  installed release.
- Use friendly user-facing errors without stack traces or internal details.
- Do not add desktop shortcuts, arbitrary install paths, or automatic launch
  after installation unless the product requirements explicitly change.
- Do not redistribute Among Us or imply affiliation with Innersloth.
